1
00:00:01,835 --> 00:00:04,904
Hey, where has Akira gone?

2
00:00:04,971 --> 00:00:05,939
I don't know.

3
00:00:06,006 --> 00:00:08,208
He wrote,
"I'm on a trip. Don't look for me."

4
00:00:08,274 --> 00:00:11,478
<i>I'm on a trip. Don't look for me.</i>

5
00:00:11,544 --> 00:00:13,813
He has been disappearing
pretty often lately.

6
00:00:13,880 --> 00:00:18,284
And saying, "Don't look for me,"
sounds like he wants us to!

7
00:00:18,351 --> 00:00:19,419
Is he hiding something?

8
00:00:19,486 --> 00:00:24,124
Maybe he left because you won
with a <i>yakuman</i> hand yesterday.

9
00:00:24,190 --> 00:00:26,126
That would be really spiteful!

10
00:00:26,192 --> 00:00:28,194
- Oh, Akira!
- Welcome back!

11
00:00:28,795 --> 00:00:29,763
Made you look!

12
00:00:30,530 --> 00:00:32,198
- Hey!
- Thank you.

13
00:00:32,699 --> 00:00:34,768
What a greedy woman you are!

14
00:00:34,834 --> 00:00:36,236
You're the greedy one!

15
00:00:36,302 --> 00:00:38,705
You've had six pieces. I've only had five.

16
00:00:38,772 --> 00:00:40,073
You were counting?

17
00:00:40,140 --> 00:00:41,641
- Yes, I was.
- You're so petty!

18
00:00:41,708 --> 00:00:44,878
Petty? What? I'm petty?

19
00:00:44,944 --> 00:00:46,079
- I'm leaving!
- Petty!

20
00:00:46,146 --> 00:00:47,547
I'm done! I'm leaving!

21
00:00:47,614 --> 00:00:48,448
That's so petty!

22
00:00:48,515 --> 00:00:51,584
<i>This is the story</i>
<i>of a maverick woman doctor.</i>

23
00:00:51,651 --> 00:00:54,387
Delicious! It's only a vegetable,
but it's delicious!

24
00:00:54,454 --> 00:00:56,189
<i>2021.</i>

25
00:00:56,256 --> 00:00:59,559
<i>The ravages</i>
<i>of a once-in-a-century pandemic</i>

26
00:00:59,626 --> 00:01:02,162
<i>have devastated</i>
<i>the world's medical systems.</i>

27
00:01:02,228 --> 00:01:03,196
Okay.

28
00:01:03,263 --> 00:01:05,298
<i>With the might of a cornered animal,</i>

29
00:01:05,365 --> 00:01:07,233
<i>Japan's medical universities</i>

30
00:01:07,734 --> 00:01:10,370
<i>have somehow weathered the storm.</i>

31
00:01:10,937 --> 00:01:15,975
This is a model of the proposed
Infection Research Center.

32
00:01:16,042 --> 00:01:17,877
If this project succeeds,

33
00:01:17,944 --> 00:01:22,916
the lives of millions of people worldwide
can be saved in the future.

34
00:01:22,982 --> 00:01:24,784
Absolutely magnificent.

35
00:01:26,619 --> 00:01:29,889
But if the government doesn't believe

36
00:01:29,956 --> 00:01:34,661
that infectious disease research
can make money, it won't fund it.

37
00:01:34,727 --> 00:01:41,167
It is for this reason that Japan was late
in developing a COVID vaccine.

38
00:01:41,768 --> 00:01:46,106
I don't want
the same mistake to happen again.

39
00:01:47,307 --> 00:01:48,608
I promise you this.

40
00:01:49,309 --> 00:01:50,844
The Ministry of Health

41
00:01:50,910 --> 00:01:53,780
will put everything it has
into supporting this project.

42
00:01:53,847 --> 00:01:54,914
Thank you.

43
00:01:54,981 --> 00:01:56,783
I'm very much looking forward

44
00:01:56,850 --> 00:01:59,252
to the emergence of a new, young leader!

45
00:02:00,954 --> 00:02:03,890
I will need your assistance.
Continue to work with me.

46
00:02:09,028 --> 00:02:11,131
Whether this succeeds or not

47
00:02:11,197 --> 00:02:13,533
depends on
the Ministry of Health's funding.

48
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:14,868
I wouldn't be so sure.

49
00:02:15,602 --> 00:02:17,604
You see, I'm a slave to my wife.

50
00:02:18,838 --> 00:02:20,907
Oh, you. Don't talk
like that at my workplace.

51
00:02:22,642 --> 00:02:23,576
<i>Meanwhile,</i>

52
00:02:23,643 --> 00:02:26,346
<i>this freelance maverick doctor,</i>

53
00:02:26,412 --> 00:02:30,517
<i>who was never attached</i>
<i>to any hospital, returned.</i>

54
00:02:33,686 --> 00:02:35,889
Who's the handsome guy
in Dr. Daimon's usual seat?

55
00:02:35,955 --> 00:02:37,690
I'm wondering too.

56
00:02:37,757 --> 00:02:39,659
He's such a cutie!

57
00:02:39,726 --> 00:02:41,461
Could he be her boyfriend?

58
00:02:42,295 --> 00:02:43,463
Of course not!

59
00:02:43,530 --> 00:02:45,031
Dr. Daimon is an old woman!

60
00:02:45,698 --> 00:02:47,600
What?

61
00:02:47,667 --> 00:02:49,335
Who are you calling "old woman"?

62
00:02:49,402 --> 00:02:50,670
What?

63
00:02:50,737 --> 00:02:52,305
Want me to pull your tongue out?

64
00:02:52,372 --> 00:02:54,240
- It's the truth though.
- What?

65
00:02:54,307 --> 00:02:56,009
- I was lying!
- What?

66
00:02:56,075 --> 00:02:57,443
I was lying!

67
00:02:58,344 --> 00:02:59,512
Hey, you.

68
00:03:00,113 --> 00:03:01,848
That's my seat.

69
00:03:04,150 --> 00:03:05,418
I've been wanting to meet you.

70
00:03:05,485 --> 00:03:06,419
What?

71
00:03:06,486 --> 00:03:08,154
He confessed his love.

72
00:03:08,221 --> 00:03:09,455
Could this be forbidden love?

73
00:03:09,522 --> 00:03:11,090
Who the heck are you?

74
00:03:11,624 --> 00:03:13,126
It has been a while.

75
00:03:13,193 --> 00:03:14,694
Like I said, who are you?

76
00:03:14,761 --> 00:03:16,996
I would like to ask
Dr. Jonouchi something.

77
00:03:17,597 --> 00:03:18,498
Dr. Jonouchi?

78
00:03:18,565 --> 00:03:19,899
Or maybe not.

79
00:03:20,867 --> 00:03:22,402
My mother didn't want me to.

80
00:03:25,805 --> 00:03:26,639
Let me see this.

81
00:03:27,207 --> 00:03:28,208
Go ahead.

82
00:03:29,676 --> 00:03:31,477
MEDICAL CHART
SATSUKI YAGAMI

83
00:03:33,179 --> 00:03:35,215
- Is this your mother?
- Yes.

84
00:03:35,782 --> 00:03:38,585
Stage 4B multiple pancreatic
neuroendocrine tumors

85
00:03:38,651 --> 00:03:39,852
and liver metastasis.

86
00:03:40,587 --> 00:03:41,721
Let me operate.

87
00:03:42,422 --> 00:03:43,423
What?

88
00:03:43,489 --> 00:03:44,757
She can be cured?

89
00:03:44,824 --> 00:03:45,858
Yuki?

90
00:03:47,927 --> 00:03:49,295
There you are.

91
00:03:50,897 --> 00:03:51,731
Wait…

92
00:03:51,798 --> 00:03:52,966
Are you Dr. Jonouchi?

93
00:03:53,032 --> 00:03:54,634
No, I'm not.

94
00:03:55,268 --> 00:03:57,403
I am Hiromi Jonouchi.

95
00:03:58,571 --> 00:03:59,539
I'm sorry!

96
00:04:00,073 --> 00:04:01,207
It's okay.

97
00:04:05,612 --> 00:04:06,613
Hiromi!

98
00:04:06,679 --> 00:04:08,047
Satsuki.

99
00:04:08,114 --> 00:04:10,617
- I'm sorry for showing up suddenly.
- It's okay.

100
00:04:11,117 --> 00:04:13,987
You haven't changed a single bit.

101
00:04:14,053 --> 00:04:16,456
- You haven't either, Hiromi.
- Oh, hardly.

102
00:04:16,522 --> 00:04:17,824
How many years has it been?

103
00:04:18,424 --> 00:04:21,194
We last met at your wedding,

104
00:04:21,794 --> 00:04:23,663
so maybe 15 years.

105
00:04:24,230 --> 00:04:25,598
I guess you're right.

106
00:04:25,665 --> 00:04:26,966
I got divorced though.

107
00:04:27,033 --> 00:04:28,601
Yours lasted longer than mine.

108
00:04:28,668 --> 00:04:30,103
Oh, not at all.

109
00:04:30,169 --> 00:04:33,606
Back then, Yuki was only this big.

110
00:04:33,673 --> 00:04:35,408
I hardly recognized him.

111
00:04:47,453 --> 00:04:49,989
Why did you let it get this bad?

112
00:04:51,424 --> 00:04:53,293
I've been to several hospitals.

113
00:04:53,893 --> 00:04:55,161
Are you getting treatment?

114
00:04:56,396 --> 00:04:59,299
It was brutal
and it wasn't having any effect.

115
00:04:59,365 --> 00:05:00,933
You need to get treatment!

116
00:05:02,135 --> 00:05:04,837
I know very well
that I don't have much longer.

117
00:05:05,438 --> 00:05:06,439
So…

118
00:05:06,973 --> 00:05:10,510
I wanted to enjoy the time I have left.

119
00:05:12,178 --> 00:05:17,350
But Yuki has insisted that I try
getting treatment one more time.

120
00:05:18,484 --> 00:05:19,352
I looked into it

121
00:05:19,952 --> 00:05:22,522
and saw that this hospital
does chemical surgery.

122
00:05:23,489 --> 00:05:25,191
I thought it might cure her.

123
00:05:25,792 --> 00:05:26,626
I see.

124
00:05:27,126 --> 00:05:29,295
Then I saw that you work here.

125
00:05:31,197 --> 00:05:33,566
I think this is fate.

126
00:05:36,402 --> 00:05:38,438
I'll think of everything that can be done.

127
00:05:43,109 --> 00:05:44,243
Let's fight this together.

128
00:05:45,411 --> 00:05:46,612
Thank you!

129
00:05:48,047 --> 00:05:51,951
<i>She hates groups,</i>

130
00:05:52,018 --> 00:05:53,019
<i>she hates authorities,</i>

131
00:05:53,086 --> 00:05:54,887
<i>and she hates constraints.</i>

132
00:05:55,488 --> 00:05:58,624
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill</i>

133
00:05:58,691 --> 00:06:00,560
<i>to work her way up.</i>

134
00:06:01,494 --> 00:06:03,796
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

135
00:06:03,863 --> 00:06:06,999
<i>Also known as… Doctor X.</i>

136
00:06:29,288 --> 00:06:31,391
I am really starving!

137
00:06:36,195 --> 00:06:37,363
Construction?

138
00:06:39,499 --> 00:06:40,933
BUILDING NEW RESEARCH CENTER

139
00:06:41,734 --> 00:06:42,735
Hey!

140
00:06:42,802 --> 00:06:45,071
How come I can't go in there?

141
00:06:46,606 --> 00:06:49,475
Don't bow to me! Answer my question!

142
00:06:52,478 --> 00:06:53,312
Hey!

143
00:06:53,379 --> 00:06:54,213
Oh, hey!

144
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:57,917
- Well, if it isn't Dr. Daimon.
- Yes?

145
00:07:00,820 --> 00:07:03,256
- Thank you for the other day.
- Sure.

146
00:07:03,823 --> 00:07:07,293
This was a shortcut to the cafeteria.
Why is it blocked off?

147
00:07:07,894 --> 00:07:11,264
Beyond there is my dream.

148
00:07:11,330 --> 00:07:12,398
What?

149
00:07:12,465 --> 00:07:13,733
I have an idea.

150
00:07:13,800 --> 00:07:15,768
Why don't you have look at it with me?

151
00:07:15,835 --> 00:07:16,969
I won't.

152
00:07:17,570 --> 00:07:19,572
Dreams won't fill my belly.

153
00:07:19,639 --> 00:07:24,277
The Infection Research Center
is the hope of humanity.

154
00:07:24,977 --> 00:07:29,715
I would like to talk to you
about future patients.

155
00:07:29,782 --> 00:07:32,151
I'm all about my next patient…

156
00:07:32,919 --> 00:07:34,687
and my next meal!

157
00:07:38,958 --> 00:07:42,495
The patient, Satsuki Yagami,
has a three-centimeter tumor…

158
00:07:42,562 --> 00:07:44,931
on the pancreas head and duodenum…

159
00:07:45,631 --> 00:07:48,334
which has metastasized
to 12 places on both liver lobes.

160
00:07:48,401 --> 00:07:50,436
She cannot be treated surgically.

161
00:07:51,204 --> 00:07:54,474
The only treatment option
is chemical surgery.

162
00:07:55,575 --> 00:07:58,578
Hepatic artery chemoembolization
is a possibility,

163
00:07:58,644 --> 00:08:02,949
but the patient has refused
the use of chemotherapy drugs,

164
00:08:03,015 --> 00:08:06,385
so the best treatment
is boron neutron capture therapy.

165
00:08:06,452 --> 00:08:09,155
- I wouldn't be so sure about that.
- Dr. Demon!

166
00:08:10,356 --> 00:08:13,392
While waiting for the liver's
embolized artery to dilate,

167
00:08:13,459 --> 00:08:15,862
hormone treatments
could retard tumor growth,

168
00:08:15,928 --> 00:08:17,597
so surgery is still possible.

169
00:08:17,663 --> 00:08:20,533
By your method,
the blood coagulates easily

170
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:23,035
and could cause a thromboembolism.

171
00:08:23,102 --> 00:08:25,872
That can be handled
by also administering heparin.

172
00:08:25,938 --> 00:08:27,874
What about the pancreatic tumor?

173
00:08:27,940 --> 00:08:31,310
Simultaneous partial liver,
pancreas, and duodenum resection.

174
00:08:31,377 --> 00:08:32,512
Ridiculous! That's…

175
00:08:34,046 --> 00:08:34,947
Ridiculous!

176
00:08:36,983 --> 00:08:41,621
Dr. Daimon, this patient
can't be operated on.

177
00:08:42,455 --> 00:08:43,589
How come?

178
00:08:43,656 --> 00:08:46,325
The patient has chosen chemical surgery.

179
00:08:46,826 --> 00:08:47,927
Are you serious?

180
00:08:47,994 --> 00:08:53,266
In other words, the possibility
of doing surgery is zero.

181
00:09:02,742 --> 00:09:07,847
Dr. Kuwagata, that chemical surgery
you do, it's really something.

182
00:09:07,914 --> 00:09:09,282
Thank you.

183
00:09:09,348 --> 00:09:10,349
SHIGEKATSU HIRUMA
ACTING DIRECTOR

184
00:09:10,416 --> 00:09:11,684
Eat up.

185
00:09:12,485 --> 00:09:15,021
- I do not like meat.
- What?

186
00:09:15,888 --> 00:09:18,190
You're a vegetarian? With those looks?

187
00:09:18,824 --> 00:09:21,260
- Tick me off.
- Did you just say, "Tick me off"?

188
00:09:23,129 --> 00:09:24,664
What do you want from me anyway?

189
00:09:25,164 --> 00:09:27,767
That Infection Research Center

190
00:09:27,833 --> 00:09:31,070
that Dr. Hachisuka is working on,

191
00:09:31,137 --> 00:09:34,607
will it be part
of the Totei University organization?

192
00:09:35,441 --> 00:09:37,076
Or won't it?

193
00:09:37,143 --> 00:09:39,812
I believe it will be
an international facility

194
00:09:39,879 --> 00:09:42,715
that's not affiliated
with Totei University.

195
00:09:44,517 --> 00:09:47,653
Is that right? That infection maniac.

196
00:09:47,720 --> 00:09:49,121
"Infection maniac?"

197
00:09:49,188 --> 00:09:50,156
In other words,

198
00:09:50,222 --> 00:09:56,262
Dr. Hachisuka will abandon his position
at Totei University Hospital, right?

199
00:09:57,063 --> 00:09:57,897
Most likely.

200
00:09:57,964 --> 00:09:59,632
You poor thing.

201
00:10:00,900 --> 00:10:05,471
Your long selfless devotion
to Dr. Hachisuka…

202
00:10:06,005 --> 00:10:07,640
will become meaningless.

203
00:10:09,875 --> 00:10:11,911
I was thinking the same thing.

204
00:10:14,647 --> 00:10:16,849
Well…

205
00:10:16,916 --> 00:10:18,718
May I join you?

206
00:10:18,784 --> 00:10:22,788
If you have something interesting
to tell me…

207
00:10:24,190 --> 00:10:28,194
I am not interested in anyone
who would abandon power to do research.

208
00:10:31,497 --> 00:10:36,535
May I interpret that to mean you have

209
00:10:37,136 --> 00:10:39,338
given up on Chief Hachisuka?

210
00:10:39,939 --> 00:10:41,173
Most certainly.

211
00:10:42,441 --> 00:10:45,077
I've brought you
a trustworthy proposition.

212
00:10:49,115 --> 00:10:52,351
I would like you to use
your power, Dr. Hiruma,

213
00:10:52,418 --> 00:10:55,855
to quickly cure this patient
in the utmost secrecy.

214
00:10:59,125 --> 00:10:59,992
Lung cancer.

215
00:11:00,059 --> 00:11:01,360
This is serious.

216
00:11:02,061 --> 00:11:03,262
Yes.

217
00:11:04,296 --> 00:11:07,833
Whose medical chart is this?

218
00:11:13,906 --> 00:11:15,474
Vice Minister Kanbe?

219
00:11:25,751 --> 00:11:27,053
I can't cut it!

220
00:11:27,620 --> 00:11:30,456
Akira is gone!
Jonouchi won't let me operate!

221
00:11:30,523 --> 00:11:32,124
And I can't cut this pumpkin!

222
00:11:32,692 --> 00:11:35,094
Oh, Ben Casey and Gannon!

223
00:11:35,661 --> 00:11:38,397
I'm starving!

224
00:11:38,464 --> 00:11:39,298
BEN CASEY
GANNON

225
00:11:40,900 --> 00:11:42,468
Akira!

226
00:11:43,035 --> 00:11:44,570
Welcome back!

227
00:11:44,637 --> 00:11:46,472
Dr. Daimon! Long time no see!

228
00:11:48,107 --> 00:11:51,010
I'm in town on a trip.
Let me bunk here tonight.

229
00:11:51,077 --> 00:11:52,344
- What?
- Oh, sorry.

230
00:11:52,411 --> 00:11:56,015
I've been in Akita for so long,
I'm speaking like them.

231
00:11:56,082 --> 00:11:58,150
I've come here on a trip.

232
00:11:58,217 --> 00:12:00,519
Can you let me stay? I'll sleep anywhere.

233
00:12:00,586 --> 00:12:02,555
Stay at a hotel!

234
00:12:02,621 --> 00:12:04,290
Hotels in Tokyo are expensive!

235
00:12:04,356 --> 00:12:05,925
I want to save on travel expenses.

236
00:12:05,991 --> 00:12:07,293
I got you a souvenir.

237
00:12:09,028 --> 00:12:12,231
- Is that edible?
- Of course, it is! Look!

238
00:12:12,298 --> 00:12:14,533
That's matsutake mushrooms!

239
00:12:14,600 --> 00:12:17,303
- I can hardly wait!
- They smell great.

240
00:12:17,369 --> 00:12:19,171
I bet they do.

241
00:12:22,541 --> 00:12:23,909
It's tiny.

242
00:12:23,976 --> 00:12:26,312
FAMOUS AKITA
SPECIAL MATSUTAKE MUSHROOMS

243
00:12:26,378 --> 00:12:27,646
What the…

244
00:12:27,713 --> 00:12:30,983
Do I stick with Hachi or Hiru?

245
00:12:31,050 --> 00:12:33,586
Hachi the Bee will cause
anaphylactic shock.

246
00:12:33,652 --> 00:12:35,855
Hiru the Leech will cause hemorrhaging.

247
00:12:35,921 --> 00:12:37,590
My survival depends on my choice.

248
00:12:37,656 --> 00:12:38,491
Oh, hey!

249
00:12:38,557 --> 00:12:39,792
It's Kuwa-chan!

250
00:12:40,926 --> 00:12:42,695
What's the trouble today?

251
00:12:43,195 --> 00:12:44,830
My heart has been ravaged.

252
00:12:44,897 --> 00:12:46,565
Oh, how awful!

253
00:12:46,632 --> 00:12:48,367
- You need injection!
- You need injection!

254
00:12:48,434 --> 00:12:52,104
- Give me a big shot of the usual!
- Sure thing!

255
00:12:56,475 --> 00:12:57,743
- Here it comes!
- Here it comes!

256
00:12:57,810 --> 00:12:58,978
Okay!

257
00:13:00,713 --> 00:13:03,048
Don't you know
how to give a shot, you idiot?

258
00:13:03,649 --> 00:13:04,884
You call yourself a nurse?

259
00:13:04,950 --> 00:13:07,219
- Kuwa-chan is frightening!
- Kuwa-chan is frightening!

260
00:13:07,953 --> 00:13:09,555
I'm taking over!

261
00:13:09,622 --> 00:13:10,823
Who's this old hag?

262
00:13:10,890 --> 00:13:12,458
I'm Head Nurse Shiraki.

263
00:13:13,225 --> 00:13:15,928
The "shira" in "Shiraki"
is the "white" in "virgin white"!

264
00:13:15,995 --> 00:13:17,363
- What?
- I see.

265
00:13:17,429 --> 00:13:20,533
We don't want doctors here
who insult our nurses.

266
00:13:20,599 --> 00:13:22,568
- How dare you.
- How dare you!

267
00:13:22,635 --> 00:13:27,940
It's time to kick out these idiot doctors!

268
00:13:28,674 --> 00:13:29,809
- Yes, ma'am!
- Yes, ma'am!

269
00:13:57,169 --> 00:13:58,237
Hello.

270
00:14:00,372 --> 00:14:01,540
Hey…

271
00:14:02,274 --> 00:14:03,509
Let me operate on you.

272
00:14:05,411 --> 00:14:06,245
Thank you.

273
00:14:07,179 --> 00:14:08,080
What?

274
00:14:08,147 --> 00:14:10,816
You're Dr. Daimon, right?

275
00:14:12,518 --> 00:14:13,352
Yes. So?

276
00:14:14,620 --> 00:14:17,122
I've heard about you from Hiromi.

277
00:14:18,257 --> 00:14:22,394
She says you're a super doctor
who's an incredible surgeon.

278
00:14:23,395 --> 00:14:24,563
Why, thank you.

279
00:14:27,566 --> 00:14:29,101
To be perfectly honest,

280
00:14:29,635 --> 00:14:31,103
I'm fine either way.

281
00:14:31,971 --> 00:14:34,573
Whether I get surgery or chemical surgery.

282
00:14:35,774 --> 00:14:37,576
You don't care?

283
00:14:39,011 --> 00:14:40,579
This was Yuki's decision.

284
00:14:42,982 --> 00:14:44,617
You know what he told me?

285
00:14:46,051 --> 00:14:48,454
"I don't want to regret that…"

286
00:14:51,557 --> 00:14:54,226
"I didn't try my hardest to help you."

287
00:14:56,629 --> 00:14:59,265
I couldn't help
wanting to do what he asked then.

288
00:15:03,002 --> 00:15:04,570
Are you worried about something?

289
00:15:06,138 --> 00:15:07,673
I'm not worried at all.

290
00:15:08,274 --> 00:15:09,708
I'm not getting surgery.

291
00:15:13,512 --> 00:15:17,917
I'm only doing what he wants me to do.

292
00:15:19,285 --> 00:15:20,219
That's what I decided.

293
00:15:23,422 --> 00:15:24,990
Do you understand?

294
00:15:27,960 --> 00:15:29,028
Will you leave now?

295
00:15:34,500 --> 00:15:35,768
I'll be back.

296
00:15:44,643 --> 00:15:47,513
- Are you fighting with her?
- We're always like this.

297
00:15:49,581 --> 00:15:51,684
Just like us when we were in high school.

298
00:15:52,551 --> 00:15:53,385
What?

299
00:15:54,353 --> 00:15:56,755
You can fight
when you're friends with someone.

300
00:16:02,294 --> 00:16:04,063
Let's start your treatment.

301
00:16:09,001 --> 00:16:10,569
I'll inject you with midazolam.

302
00:16:11,270 --> 00:16:14,840
Satsuki, you'll fall asleep.

303
00:16:14,907 --> 00:16:15,908
Okay.

304
00:16:16,976 --> 00:16:20,245
We will now begin the neutron irradiation

305
00:16:20,312 --> 00:16:22,414
for boron neutron capture therapy.

306
00:16:22,481 --> 00:16:24,016
Start the irradiation.

307
00:16:25,884 --> 00:16:27,319
- Start!
- Yes, sir.

308
00:16:39,331 --> 00:16:42,768
I hear the Infection Research Center
construction…

309
00:16:42,835 --> 00:16:44,203
is going smoothly.

310
00:16:44,903 --> 00:16:46,705
I swear it will be a success.

311
00:16:46,772 --> 00:16:49,608
The medical department
in a university hospital

312
00:16:49,675 --> 00:16:51,710
is a hierarchic society
with unshakable fetters.

313
00:16:52,311 --> 00:16:53,145
Right?

314
00:16:53,679 --> 00:16:57,316
When those below you cooperate
and help you,

315
00:16:57,916 --> 00:16:59,418
you can remain a leader.

316
00:17:00,486 --> 00:17:04,123
I can only hope that your position
doesn't become…

317
00:17:04,723 --> 00:17:07,860
a house built on sand.

318
00:17:10,996 --> 00:17:14,333
Thank you very much for the warning.

319
00:17:16,301 --> 00:17:17,302
You can't go in!

320
00:17:17,369 --> 00:17:20,472
- It's all right!
- He is in a meeting!

321
00:17:20,539 --> 00:17:22,574
Acting Director Hiruma!

322
00:17:22,641 --> 00:17:24,309
It has been a while!

323
00:17:24,376 --> 00:17:26,111
Chief Hachisuka is here too?

324
00:17:26,178 --> 00:17:27,146
Hello.

325
00:17:27,746 --> 00:17:29,381
- I'll be going.
- Okay. Bye.

326
00:17:30,182 --> 00:17:33,685
He's as rude as ever.
How can he still be chief?

327
00:17:33,752 --> 00:17:35,020
- Dr. Ebina.
- Yes?

328
00:17:35,621 --> 00:17:40,926
You've always got impeccable
and perfect timing!

329
00:17:40,993 --> 00:17:42,327
Thank you!

330
00:17:42,394 --> 00:17:44,496
- Anyway, have a seat.
- Thank you.

331
00:17:44,563 --> 00:17:45,431
Go ahead.

332
00:17:45,931 --> 00:17:47,900
This is a souvenir.

333
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:51,270
"Famous Akita
special Matsutake mushrooms."

334
00:17:51,336 --> 00:17:52,805
I bet it's big.

335
00:17:54,139 --> 00:17:56,008
- Yes…
- Matsutake.

336
00:17:57,042 --> 00:17:58,077
- Dr. Ebina.
- Yes?

337
00:17:59,244 --> 00:18:03,715
Would you like to return
to the main Totei University Hospital?

338
00:18:04,583 --> 00:18:05,417
Yes.

339
00:18:05,951 --> 00:18:07,252
Leave it to me.

340
00:18:07,920 --> 00:18:09,621
SURGERY DEPARTMENT

341
00:18:09,688 --> 00:18:11,557
Hello, everyone! Long time no see!

342
00:18:11,623 --> 00:18:14,526
- Woah!
- How have you been?

343
00:18:14,593 --> 00:18:15,427
Hey!

344
00:18:15,494 --> 00:18:17,396
Former Director Ebina, have you returned?

345
00:18:17,463 --> 00:18:19,965
- Welcome back!
- No, not yet.

346
00:18:20,032 --> 00:18:22,734
These are Akita specialty
Namahage sweet buns.

347
00:18:23,435 --> 00:18:26,171
Just one each though! One each.

348
00:18:30,442 --> 00:18:32,644
- Hara?
- It has been a while.

349
00:18:32,711 --> 00:18:35,013
- What are you doing here?
- I returned.

350
00:18:35,080 --> 00:18:37,349
- Why are you here?
- Stuff happened.

351
00:18:38,350 --> 00:18:39,651
Is that right?

352
00:18:39,718 --> 00:18:41,720
It's nice that you can return
after "stuff happened."

353
00:18:43,355 --> 00:18:46,391
- What's up?
- Oh, well…

354
00:18:46,458 --> 00:18:48,193
- Let me ask you something.
- No thank you.

355
00:18:48,260 --> 00:18:50,429
- I haven't said anything yet!
- I know.

356
00:18:50,496 --> 00:18:52,264
That's an incredibly difficult operation.

357
00:18:52,831 --> 00:18:54,166
- You're going to do this?
- Yes.

358
00:18:54,233 --> 00:18:57,035
If I do this, Acting Director Hiruma said…

359
00:18:57,636 --> 00:18:59,505
he would bring me back
to the main hospital.

360
00:19:00,239 --> 00:19:01,640
Can you do this, Dr. Ebina?

361
00:19:01,707 --> 00:19:04,943
Of course, I can't.
Only one person can do it.

362
00:19:05,010 --> 00:19:06,612
You mean me?

363
00:19:06,678 --> 00:19:08,013
With those looks,

364
00:19:08,614 --> 00:19:11,083
I didn't know you told jokes like that.

365
00:19:11,150 --> 00:19:12,284
It's not a joke.

366
00:19:14,453 --> 00:19:16,255
Kin-chan! There you are!

367
00:19:16,321 --> 00:19:17,623
I've been found!

368
00:19:18,790 --> 00:19:20,859
I'm Dr. Ebina. You can call me Ebi-chan.

369
00:19:20,926 --> 00:19:22,728
Ebi-chan! There you are!

370
00:19:22,794 --> 00:19:26,431
Would you like the usual injection?

371
00:19:26,498 --> 00:19:27,833
Don't hurt me.

372
00:19:29,568 --> 00:19:30,769
- That's how you do it?
- Yes.

373
00:19:30,836 --> 00:19:32,171
Don't hurt me.

374
00:19:34,039 --> 00:19:36,141
Here it comes!

375
00:19:36,742 --> 00:19:38,043
Let me take over.

376
00:19:38,544 --> 00:19:40,646
- It's… Head Nurse Shiraki!
- Head Nurse Shiraki!

377
00:19:40,712 --> 00:19:43,148
I'm glad to see you're both well.

378
00:19:43,215 --> 00:19:44,816
Why are you here, Ms. Shiraki?

379
00:19:44,883 --> 00:19:47,920
I worked at Totei University
Hospital until retirement,

380
00:19:48,554 --> 00:19:50,322
but I can't quit this kind of work.

381
00:19:50,389 --> 00:19:51,924
This job seems a bit different.

382
00:19:51,990 --> 00:19:56,094
What's more, the doctors who come here
get worse all the time!

383
00:19:56,161 --> 00:19:57,462
It's deplorable!

384
00:19:57,529 --> 00:19:59,131
Open your mouth! Here!

385
00:19:59,198 --> 00:20:00,332
Here!

386
00:20:01,099 --> 00:20:01,967
There!

387
00:20:04,236 --> 00:20:06,038
PATIENT NAME: SATSUKI YAGAMI

388
00:20:14,947 --> 00:20:18,050
Oh, it's getting smaller.
I guess it's working.

389
00:20:18,717 --> 00:20:20,352
But we can't rest easy yet.

390
00:20:21,520 --> 00:20:22,521
Yes.

391
00:20:23,055 --> 00:20:25,157
It's easier to operate on than before.

392
00:20:25,224 --> 00:20:28,193
If you operate now,
it's more likely to succeed.

393
00:20:28,260 --> 00:20:29,428
I know that.

394
00:20:31,630 --> 00:20:33,165
I know that if you operate,

395
00:20:33,699 --> 00:20:36,134
her chances would improve a lot.

396
00:20:40,072 --> 00:20:41,406
But…

397
00:20:42,074 --> 00:20:46,378
all the hospitals she went to
told her surgery wouldn't work.

398
00:20:47,312 --> 00:20:50,782
So Yuki looked everywhere for a cure…

399
00:20:50,849 --> 00:20:53,952
and finally found
the chemical surgery we offer here.

400
00:20:57,089 --> 00:20:59,358
Respecting a patient's decision is also…

401
00:21:01,526 --> 00:21:02,628
a doctor's job.

402
00:21:09,101 --> 00:21:11,837
So don't try to do anything
without asking.

403
00:21:16,308 --> 00:21:19,311
Fine. I won't.

404
00:21:29,021 --> 00:21:29,888
Excuse me.

405
00:21:31,423 --> 00:21:32,758
Yuki.

406
00:21:38,530 --> 00:21:39,364
Dr. Daimon.

407
00:21:39,431 --> 00:21:43,101
Actually, there's a surgery
I want you to do.

408
00:21:43,168 --> 00:21:45,070
- Sure.
- Really?

409
00:21:45,137 --> 00:21:47,306
That was fast!

410
00:21:47,372 --> 00:21:50,375
I've never seen that!
I thought she would refuse.

411
00:21:51,510 --> 00:21:52,778
Knock-knock.

412
00:21:54,446 --> 00:21:55,847
I knew you would be back.

413
00:21:55,914 --> 00:21:57,416
I don't give up.

414
00:21:58,350 --> 00:21:59,918
Keep coming, but my answer won't change.

415
00:22:00,519 --> 00:22:02,921
- I'm not getting surgery.
- You will get surgery.

416
00:22:03,789 --> 00:22:05,057
Let me operate.

417
00:22:06,224 --> 00:22:07,626
You sure are stubborn.

418
00:22:08,226 --> 00:22:09,861
You're just like Hiromi.

419
00:22:10,429 --> 00:22:11,396
Give me a break.

420
00:22:12,364 --> 00:22:14,633
But I'm not one to talk.

421
00:22:16,968 --> 00:22:18,637
In high school,

422
00:22:18,704 --> 00:22:20,272
we fought over a guy.

423
00:22:21,373 --> 00:22:22,641
Really?

424
00:22:22,708 --> 00:22:24,009
Is that right?

425
00:22:25,477 --> 00:22:27,145
He was a hot-looking classmate.

426
00:22:27,746 --> 00:22:30,015
He was on the soccer team
and everyone admired him.

427
00:22:30,082 --> 00:22:31,083
Really?

428
00:22:32,918 --> 00:22:34,753
Neither of us would give up.

429
00:22:35,487 --> 00:22:37,789
We stopped talking to each other
for a while.

430
00:22:37,856 --> 00:22:39,925
So who won?

431
00:22:41,259 --> 00:22:42,527
In the end,

432
00:22:43,528 --> 00:22:45,297
Hiromi let me have him.

433
00:22:45,864 --> 00:22:46,798
Seriously?

434
00:22:47,399 --> 00:22:50,135
That girl absolutely hates losing.

435
00:22:50,202 --> 00:22:53,605
I had the bigger boobs, after all.

436
00:22:54,106 --> 00:22:55,741
- Boobs?
- Yes.

437
00:22:56,908 --> 00:22:59,411
Oh, I see.

438
00:23:00,412 --> 00:23:03,115
He and I had Yuki.

439
00:23:05,851 --> 00:23:07,152
In my senior year of high school.

440
00:23:07,219 --> 00:23:08,420
Your senior year?

441
00:23:09,788 --> 00:23:12,124
I guess she had no choice but to give up.

442
00:23:13,392 --> 00:23:15,961
But it caused a huge ruckus at school.

443
00:23:16,762 --> 00:23:19,464
I was almost kicked out of school.

444
00:23:20,899 --> 00:23:22,334
At that time,

445
00:23:22,401 --> 00:23:26,071
the one who fought
with the school the hardest was Hiromi.

446
00:23:28,507 --> 00:23:31,943
It's thanks to Hiromi
that I even graduated.

447
00:23:32,511 --> 00:23:33,345
I see.

448
00:23:37,449 --> 00:23:39,818
I heard I'm getting better.

449
00:23:41,420 --> 00:23:42,487
Yes.

450
00:23:45,123 --> 00:23:47,492
Not only did Hiromi give me her man,

451
00:23:48,693 --> 00:23:50,529
but she has given me hope for life.

452
00:23:54,533 --> 00:23:58,003
I've got nothing but thanks for Hiromi.

453
00:24:05,043 --> 00:24:07,345
Are you going to say something again?

454
00:24:08,246 --> 00:24:10,315
I told you I don't give up easily.

455
00:24:12,551 --> 00:24:13,985
Let me operate.

456
00:24:17,189 --> 00:24:20,025
I will not fail.

457
00:24:23,962 --> 00:24:25,030
<i>Mom…</i>

458
00:24:26,097 --> 00:24:28,433
got divorced when I was two.

459
00:24:33,438 --> 00:24:35,173
To raise me,

460
00:24:36,141 --> 00:24:38,410
she sacrificed her own life.

461
00:24:42,380 --> 00:24:43,448
From now on…

462
00:24:46,585 --> 00:24:48,286
I want her to live for herself.

463
00:24:51,590 --> 00:24:52,858
For as long as she can.

464
00:24:57,863 --> 00:24:59,664
I'm sure she can also find love again.

465
00:25:01,299 --> 00:25:02,434
You're right.

466
00:25:02,968 --> 00:25:04,503
Satsuki is very beautiful.

467
00:25:06,371 --> 00:25:08,139
She can find lots of lovers.

468
00:25:08,707 --> 00:25:10,909
She could even get two
or three men at once.

469
00:25:10,976 --> 00:25:12,677
What? I can't allow that!

470
00:25:12,744 --> 00:25:16,414
How come? You said
you want her to be happy, right?

471
00:25:17,849 --> 00:25:20,018
<i>I've secretly reserved an OR.</i>

472
00:25:20,085 --> 00:25:24,322
Vice Minister Kanbe's condition
won't be leaked.

473
00:25:24,389 --> 00:25:25,690
Does Chief Hachisuka know?

474
00:25:26,191 --> 00:25:27,392
No, definitely not.

475
00:25:28,059 --> 00:25:29,461
If he found out,

476
00:25:30,061 --> 00:25:31,596
then we would be through for sure.

477
00:25:31,663 --> 00:25:33,765
Then we would abandon him first.

478
00:25:33,832 --> 00:25:35,433
That's all it would take.

479
00:25:36,134 --> 00:25:38,503
Do you always want to be
Hachisuka's jerk's dog?

480
00:25:39,504 --> 00:25:40,872
Arf, arf!

481
00:25:41,740 --> 00:25:42,774
Before long,

482
00:25:43,708 --> 00:25:45,076
you need to take a stand.

483
00:25:49,848 --> 00:25:52,217
We will now conduct
a right upper lung lobectomy

484
00:25:52,284 --> 00:25:54,886
and mediastinal lymph node dissection.

485
00:25:54,953 --> 00:25:56,688
- Let's begin.
- Yes, sir.

486
00:25:56,755 --> 00:25:57,956
- Scalpel.
- Here.

487
00:26:02,894 --> 00:26:04,529
- Bovie.
- Here.

488
00:26:11,336 --> 00:26:14,706
I never thought I would operate
with you again. I'm counting on you.

489
00:26:14,773 --> 00:26:16,541
Let's get this over fast.

490
00:26:16,608 --> 00:26:17,676
Right.

491
00:26:18,610 --> 00:26:20,545
- I'm getting excited.
- Get to work already.

492
00:26:20,612 --> 00:26:21,880
Right. Hooked forceps.

493
00:26:24,516 --> 00:26:28,820
It figures the stand-in doctor
is Dr. Michiko Daimon.

494
00:26:28,887 --> 00:26:30,121
She's really something.

495
00:26:30,689 --> 00:26:32,490
I can rest easy now.

496
00:26:35,293 --> 00:26:38,330
Maybe I'll have meat again tonight.

497
00:26:42,067 --> 00:26:43,602
From the very start,

498
00:26:43,668 --> 00:26:45,537
you wanted Dr. Michiko Daimon to operate.

499
00:26:46,137 --> 00:26:48,173
That's why you asked
Acting Director Hiruma.

500
00:26:48,873 --> 00:26:51,142
It doesn't always seem like it,

501
00:26:51,743 --> 00:26:53,244
but you want to save your husband.

502
00:26:53,845 --> 00:26:54,679
No.

503
00:26:54,746 --> 00:26:56,081
Who I want to save is…

504
00:26:56,948 --> 00:26:59,851
the Ministry of Health's Vice Minister…

505
00:27:01,486 --> 00:27:03,855
who will give our hospital
lots of funding.

506
00:27:17,769 --> 00:27:18,870
Hiromi.

507
00:27:18,937 --> 00:27:19,938
How are you feeling?

508
00:27:20,438 --> 00:27:21,473
Any changes?

509
00:27:22,073 --> 00:27:24,676
What brings you here this late at night?

510
00:27:25,610 --> 00:27:28,747
When I was going through my photos,
I found a nice one.

511
00:27:29,381 --> 00:27:30,548
What photo?

512
00:27:31,783 --> 00:27:32,751
This.

513
00:27:32,817 --> 00:27:34,386
GRADUATION CEREMONY

514
00:27:34,452 --> 00:27:36,755
Oh, wow!

515
00:27:36,821 --> 00:27:38,657
My belly was really big.

516
00:27:38,723 --> 00:27:40,992
Yuki was born ten days later.

517
00:27:41,693 --> 00:27:42,827
Oh, that's right!

518
00:27:43,328 --> 00:27:45,864
It was a really difficult delivery!

519
00:27:46,364 --> 00:27:48,900
He held my hand during that time,

520
00:27:49,501 --> 00:27:52,303
but I crushed his hand when I squeezed it.

521
00:27:53,438 --> 00:27:54,873
You mean he was present at the birth?

522
00:27:55,473 --> 00:27:56,908
He was there then.

523
00:27:57,475 --> 00:28:00,645
But it ended between us two years later.

524
00:28:04,916 --> 00:28:06,885
I had even stolen him from you.

525
00:28:07,819 --> 00:28:09,320
Pathetic, isn't it?

526
00:28:10,488 --> 00:28:12,123
Things happen.

527
00:28:15,727 --> 00:28:18,129
You're as kind as ever.

528
00:28:18,697 --> 00:28:19,664
Really?

529
00:28:20,965 --> 00:28:23,134
Even then, you were kind…

530
00:28:23,868 --> 00:28:25,570
and intelligent.

531
00:28:26,438 --> 00:28:30,141
I wished I could best you
in at least one thing.

532
00:28:33,845 --> 00:28:36,448
If I hadn't been persistent back then,

533
00:28:37,348 --> 00:28:39,684
I wonder what my life
would have been like.

534
00:28:45,390 --> 00:28:47,792
Yuki wouldn't have been in it.

535
00:28:50,762 --> 00:28:52,630
Having a great kid like him…

536
00:28:54,132 --> 00:28:56,401
is all because you worked
so hard, Satsuki.

537
00:29:07,479 --> 00:29:08,713
Yes…

538
00:29:11,082 --> 00:29:12,417
I guess you're right.

539
00:29:15,353 --> 00:29:16,688
It was for the best.

540
00:29:18,690 --> 00:29:19,891
Yes.

541
00:29:26,564 --> 00:29:27,398
Hey,

542
00:29:27,932 --> 00:29:29,901
why don't you let
Dr. Daimon operate on you?

543
00:29:30,969 --> 00:29:31,903
What?

544
00:29:32,504 --> 00:29:33,872
Your tumor has shrunk.

545
00:29:34,739 --> 00:29:37,776
I think it's worth risking surgery now.

546
00:29:40,812 --> 00:29:41,880
I see.

547
00:29:44,983 --> 00:29:46,918
Dr. Daimon is a doctor you can trust.

548
00:29:48,052 --> 00:29:51,823
<i>She even saved my life once</i>
<i>when I had cancer</i>

549
00:29:51,890 --> 00:29:53,591
<i>and had given up on life.</i>

550
00:29:55,193 --> 00:29:56,928
I never knew that.

551
00:29:58,930 --> 00:30:00,064
She…

552
00:30:01,533 --> 00:30:02,867
will not fail.

553
00:30:09,641 --> 00:30:10,842
You're right.

554
00:30:15,580 --> 00:30:18,750
There's one thing I've hidden from you.

555
00:30:20,819 --> 00:30:22,520
What? Why tell me about it now?

556
00:30:23,454 --> 00:30:25,390
I went after him hard too.

557
00:30:26,224 --> 00:30:27,058
What?

558
00:30:30,128 --> 00:30:33,198
I kissed him before you ever did.

559
00:30:34,933 --> 00:30:37,902
- I knew that.
- What?

560
00:30:37,969 --> 00:30:39,871
He told me.

561
00:30:39,938 --> 00:30:42,073
You're kidding! What a blabbermouth!

562
00:30:42,140 --> 00:30:43,641
That's for sure.

563
00:30:44,242 --> 00:30:46,678
Why the heck did we fight over that guy?

564
00:30:46,744 --> 00:30:50,081
Good point! The rashness
of youth is frightening!

565
00:30:54,552 --> 00:30:55,587
Satsuki?

566
00:30:57,055 --> 00:30:57,889
Satsuki!

567
00:31:05,597 --> 00:31:07,332
Next, I'll ablate the superior vena cava.

568
00:31:07,398 --> 00:31:08,399
- Pean.
- Here.

569
00:31:09,834 --> 00:31:12,270
- Open it wider.
- Right. I'm on it.

570
00:31:12,337 --> 00:31:13,671
Tupfer.

571
00:31:20,578 --> 00:31:22,614
BP down to the 60s.

572
00:31:22,680 --> 00:31:24,048
Pulse 130!

573
00:31:24,115 --> 00:31:25,283
Suctioning!

574
00:31:25,850 --> 00:31:26,818
What's going on?

575
00:31:28,453 --> 00:31:30,154
The superior vena cava has been damaged!

576
00:31:30,221 --> 00:31:31,923
Why does this always happen?

577
00:31:31,990 --> 00:31:33,558
- Suction for me.
- Right.

578
00:31:33,625 --> 00:31:35,827
I'll ligate the superior pulmonary artery.

579
00:31:35,894 --> 00:31:37,795
- Kelly.
- Here.

580
00:31:37,862 --> 00:31:39,597
- Prep 5-0 monofilament.
- Right.

581
00:31:39,664 --> 00:31:41,532
Give me the 5-0.

582
00:32:02,620 --> 00:32:03,922
Dr. Jonouchi!

583
00:32:06,357 --> 00:32:09,027
- Set it to DC 150!
- Got it!

584
00:32:16,501 --> 00:32:17,835
Here goes!

585
00:32:23,708 --> 00:32:24,842
How did this happen?

586
00:32:25,777 --> 00:32:27,445
Acute myocardial infarction?

587
00:32:27,512 --> 00:32:29,881
Maybe the left coronary artery
has become blocked.

588
00:32:29,948 --> 00:32:31,382
- Inject her with adrenaline!
- Right!

589
00:32:32,417 --> 00:32:33,251
Injecting.

590
00:32:39,123 --> 00:32:40,224
Here we go again.

591
00:32:43,728 --> 00:32:44,662
Her heart won't start again!

592
00:32:45,229 --> 00:32:46,264
Satsuki!

593
00:32:47,265 --> 00:32:48,299
Satsuki!

594
00:32:48,366 --> 00:32:49,500
Satsuki!

595
00:32:51,736 --> 00:32:52,870
Satsuki!

596
00:33:01,746 --> 00:33:03,781
I can't see well. More suction.

597
00:33:03,848 --> 00:33:04,983
Sorry.

598
00:33:07,218 --> 00:33:08,319
I'll finish it up.

599
00:33:08,886 --> 00:33:09,988
- Okay.
- Good.

600
00:33:28,506 --> 00:33:29,874
Mom!

601
00:33:31,275 --> 00:33:32,210
Mom?

602
00:33:37,615 --> 00:33:38,716
- Cooper.
- Here.

603
00:33:46,891 --> 00:33:49,060
BP back up to 90.

604
00:33:49,127 --> 00:33:51,062
Thank goodness!

605
00:33:51,129 --> 00:33:52,630
Thank goodness!

606
00:33:54,098 --> 00:33:56,000
I'll continue with ablation
of the right lobe.

607
00:33:56,067 --> 00:33:57,068
- Pean.
- Here.

608
00:33:57,135 --> 00:33:58,336
Dr. Daimon, sorry about that.

609
00:33:58,936 --> 00:34:00,605
If you have time to apologize,

610
00:34:00,671 --> 00:34:02,073
then open up the view more.

611
00:34:02,140 --> 00:34:03,808
Right! This time,

612
00:34:04,342 --> 00:34:05,743
I won't screw up.

613
00:34:05,810 --> 00:34:06,978
You better not!

614
00:34:26,064 --> 00:34:27,532
Come back!

615
00:34:28,933 --> 00:34:30,068
Satsuki!

616
00:34:32,670 --> 00:34:33,905
Satsuki!

617
00:34:40,845 --> 00:34:42,246
I'll take over!

618
00:34:50,154 --> 00:34:51,155
<i>Hiromi…</i>

619
00:34:52,156 --> 00:34:53,157
<i>That's enough.</i>

620
00:35:21,152 --> 00:35:22,286
Vitals?

621
00:35:22,353 --> 00:35:25,356
BP 126, pulse 82, normal sinus.

622
00:35:26,457 --> 00:35:27,291
We're done.

623
00:35:33,731 --> 00:35:35,766
- Nice work.
- Nice work.

624
00:35:35,833 --> 00:35:38,903
Thank you, Ms. Daimon.

625
00:35:54,285 --> 00:35:55,419
Dr. Daimon!

626
00:35:57,455 --> 00:35:58,556
Well…

627
00:37:08,292 --> 00:37:09,327
It's so frustrating.

628
00:37:13,364 --> 00:37:14,465
I couldn't save her.

629
00:37:21,439 --> 00:37:22,873
I couldn't do a thing.

630
00:37:32,416 --> 00:37:33,417
Thank you.

631
00:37:39,390 --> 00:37:41,592
Those are her words.

632
00:37:43,728 --> 00:37:46,497
She said, "I've got nothing
but thanks for her."

633
00:38:16,794 --> 00:38:17,895
Dr. Jonouchi.

634
00:38:27,872 --> 00:38:28,806
Yuki…

635
00:38:31,742 --> 00:38:36,080
It looked like my mother was smiling.

636
00:38:48,392 --> 00:38:50,761
Having you with her at the end…

637
00:38:54,699 --> 00:38:56,367
I'm sure that made her happy.

638
00:39:03,074 --> 00:39:04,508
Thank you.

639
00:39:32,036 --> 00:39:33,304
Yuki.

640
00:39:42,480 --> 00:39:45,750
<i>This is the story</i>
<i>of a maverick woman doctor.</i>

641
00:40:06,570 --> 00:40:07,438
A surgeon…

642
00:40:08,606 --> 00:40:11,942
can only save one patient at a time.

643
00:40:20,451 --> 00:40:24,355
That is the best a surgeon can do.

644
00:40:44,508 --> 00:40:49,046
I am terribly sorry
for the trouble I've caused you.

645
00:40:49,113 --> 00:40:51,582
You are Totei University Hospital's

646
00:40:51,649 --> 00:40:53,984
capable PR Chief, after all.

647
00:40:54,051 --> 00:40:56,487
But you used

648
00:40:56,554 --> 00:40:58,956
Dr. Michiko Daimon

649
00:40:59,023 --> 00:41:01,892
for Vice Minister Kanbe's surgery, right?

650
00:41:01,959 --> 00:41:08,132
The malicious Mr. Kambara
has something for you.

651
00:41:08,199 --> 00:41:09,133
What could it be?

652
00:41:10,367 --> 00:41:11,602
- Dr. Ebina.
- Right!

653
00:41:15,239 --> 00:41:16,807
This is a melon.

654
00:41:17,908 --> 00:41:19,009
This is the bill.

655
00:41:19,076 --> 00:41:20,277
Why are you here?

656
00:41:20,344 --> 00:41:22,546
I've returned
to Totei University Hospital.

657
00:41:23,047 --> 00:41:25,015
I brought him back.

658
00:41:27,084 --> 00:41:28,752
- May I have a look?
- Sure.

659
00:41:30,454 --> 00:41:31,622
SURGICAL FEES

660
00:41:31,689 --> 00:41:35,292
I could never pay this much.

661
00:41:35,359 --> 00:41:36,460
Is that right?

662
00:41:37,027 --> 00:41:38,362
Then…

663
00:41:39,163 --> 00:41:41,265
why don't I pay for you?

664
00:41:41,332 --> 00:41:42,366
What?

665
00:41:42,433 --> 00:41:43,968
Instead,

666
00:41:44,502 --> 00:41:46,937
I would like you…

667
00:41:48,038 --> 00:41:51,575
to carry out what you promised to do.

668
00:41:54,311 --> 00:41:55,312
Yes, sir.

669
00:41:56,080 --> 00:41:59,717
Incidentally, I'll also take this melon.

670
00:42:00,584 --> 00:42:01,986
- Yes, sir.
- What?

671
00:42:02,052 --> 00:42:03,554
- Yes, sir!
- Good.

672
00:42:04,154 --> 00:42:05,689
What do you mean it has been canceled?

673
00:42:05,756 --> 00:42:07,925
That's not what you promised!

674
00:42:07,992 --> 00:42:10,261
If the Ministry of Health stops
the research grant,

675
00:42:10,327 --> 00:42:12,563
the Infection Research Center
will be done for!

676
00:42:13,130 --> 00:42:15,099
I'm terribly sorry about this.

677
00:42:15,633 --> 00:42:16,800
Goodbye.

678
00:42:26,477 --> 00:42:27,878
What's going on here?

679
00:42:28,879 --> 00:42:29,780
I'll find out.

680
00:42:30,948 --> 00:42:32,616
That won't be necessary!

681
00:42:33,551 --> 00:42:34,451
What?

682
00:42:35,853 --> 00:42:38,822
How is your husband doing…

683
00:42:40,758 --> 00:42:41,859
after his surgery?

684
00:42:44,995 --> 00:42:49,066
If the Ministry of Health
won't provide funds,

685
00:42:50,034 --> 00:42:51,802
then it cannot be helped.

686
00:42:52,803 --> 00:42:54,171
However,

687
00:42:54,772 --> 00:42:57,341
the Infection Research Center

688
00:42:57,408 --> 00:42:59,443
is an international project.

689
00:43:00,044 --> 00:43:04,048
I can gain all the funding I need
from around the world.

690
00:43:05,382 --> 00:43:07,952
Ultimately, the ones
who will be humiliated

691
00:43:09,086 --> 00:43:11,322
will be the Ministry of Health.

692
00:43:13,490 --> 00:43:15,759
I'll need to contact

693
00:43:16,327 --> 00:43:21,498
Professor Shelp of the Safiristan Kingdom.

694
00:43:24,735 --> 00:43:25,769
Right away, sir!

695
00:43:30,674 --> 00:43:34,612
What do you mean
it's an international problem, you idiot?

696
00:43:34,678 --> 00:43:36,313
- Acting Director Hiruma.
- Yes?

697
00:43:36,380 --> 00:43:39,383
At a time like this,
let's sing "Akita Ondo" to cheer up.

698
00:43:40,651 --> 00:43:44,121
Akita's famous song, "Hachimori Hatahata."

699
00:43:44,188 --> 00:43:46,156
And Oga's song, "Buriko."

700
00:43:46,223 --> 00:43:48,759
- This is just ticking me off more!
- Sorry.

701
00:43:48,826 --> 00:43:51,195
<i>She hates groups,</i>

702
00:43:51,261 --> 00:43:53,864
<i>she hates authorities,</i>

703
00:43:53,931 --> 00:43:55,733
<i>and she hates constraints.</i>

704
00:43:55,799 --> 00:43:59,069
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill</i>

705
00:43:59,136 --> 00:44:00,671
<i>to work her way up.</i>

706
00:44:00,738 --> 00:44:02,339
That green wall again!

707
00:44:03,207 --> 00:44:06,176
Hey, hurry up and get rid of this!

708
00:44:06,243 --> 00:44:08,746
I can't get to the cafeteria.

709
00:44:08,812 --> 00:44:10,414
I'm very sorry.

710
00:44:11,315 --> 00:44:14,551
Allow me to buy you lunch.

711
00:44:14,618 --> 00:44:16,120
No thank you.

712
00:44:16,186 --> 00:44:18,322
- It's sushi.
- Sushi?

713
00:44:18,389 --> 00:44:19,790
Sushi.

714
00:44:20,724 --> 00:44:22,026
Is it…

715
00:44:22,526 --> 00:44:23,427
Yes?

716
00:44:24,628 --> 00:44:25,896
Possibly…

717
00:44:25,963 --> 00:44:27,498
"Possibly"?

718
00:44:28,065 --> 00:44:31,735
The kind that goes round and round?

719
00:44:32,936 --> 00:44:34,505
It doesn't go round.

720
00:44:36,006 --> 00:44:37,608
I would love to!

721
00:44:40,678 --> 00:44:42,980
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

722
00:44:43,047 --> 00:44:46,016
<i>Also known as… Doctor X.</i>

723
00:44:47,251 --> 00:44:49,887
That Infection Research Center!

724
00:44:49,953 --> 00:44:51,155
<i>A sushi date?</i>

725
00:44:51,221 --> 00:44:52,489
<i>That sounds serious!</i>

726
00:44:52,556 --> 00:44:53,691
<i>He has six months.</i>

727
00:44:53,757 --> 00:44:54,925
<i>No… Three months.</i>

728
00:44:54,992 --> 00:44:59,596
<i>My ideal…100% perfect treatment</i>
<i>will be realized.</i>

729
00:44:59,663 --> 00:45:01,365
<i>Isn't there something else</i>
<i>you should do first?</i>

730
00:45:01,432 --> 00:45:02,433
Subtitle translation by: Brian Athey
